+# v0.1.4 Engineering Handoff
+
+Do not begin implementation until v0.1.3 is merged, tagged, and reconciled into the planning worktree.
+
+## Starting point
+
+- Planning worktree: `/home/devansh/robotics_projects/ros2-amr-forward-planning`.
+- Planning branch: `planning/v0.1.4-v0.1.6` at `9f8072a` during this handoff.
+- The worktree contains uncommitted planning documents and a deterministic harness. Preserve that work; its old runtime source is not authoritative.
+- Harness core: `ros2_ws/src/cpp_robotics_sim_ros/test/test_support/v014_harness.py`.
+- Tests: `test/test_v014_harness_utilities.py` and `test/test_v014_mode_transition_skeleton.py`.
+- Guidance: `docs/v0.1.4_harness_integration_manifest.md`, `docs/v0.1.4_test_harness_design.md`, and `docs/v0.1.4_test_to_requirement_matrix.md` in that worktree.
+
+## Accepted v0.1.3 interfaces and invariants
+
+- `/simulation/status` and `/mode/status` remain domain status topics; `/platform/readiness` carries structured readiness; `/platform/lifecycle/transition` owns aggregate transitions.
+- Manager lifecycle state uses transient-local state/heartbeat plus the read-only `GetManagedComponentState` service.
+- Lifecycle, readiness, operating mode, and transition phase remain separate concepts.
+- ACTIVE cannot be accepted from missing, expired, wrong-runtime, inconsistent, or changed provenance. The remote lease is three seconds; aggregate success requires two stable authoritative reads.
+- v0.1.4 consumes the existing readiness profiles and preserves every failed dependency; it must not create a parallel readiness API.
+- Navigation goals remain unresolved until a terminal result. Mode changes must reject or safely cancel an active goal without fabricating completion.
+- Process signalling requires exact persisted ownership; descendants refresh before termination and shutdown converges across two scans.
+- Startup, stop, rollback, and final-verification failures remain distinct.
+- SLAM owns `map -> odom` while mapping; AMCL owns it during localization/navigation; the current controller owns `odom -> base_link` until a later tested change.
+
+## Primary files
+
+`mode_manager_node.py`, `managed_component.py`, `lifecycle_ros_adapter.py`, both platform lifecycle orchestrator files, `readiness_contract.py`, `ros_runtime_readiness.py`, `process_registry.py`, `navigation_goal_manager_node.py`, `config/mode_manager.yaml`, mode launches/tests, and the lifecycle/readiness/interface documentation.
+
+## Reconciliation sequence
+
+1. Preserve all uncommitted planning files.
+2. Fetch the accepted v0.1.3 tag and record its commit.
+3. Compare the planning branch against the tag before copying or rebasing production source.
+4. Port only isolated harness/support files onto a branch based on v0.1.3; resolve `CMakeLists.txt` test registration deliberately.
+5. Run the harness utilities and skeleton tests before implementation.
+6. Replace every `WAITING FOR V0.1.3 CONTRACT` assumption with the accepted interfaces.
+
+```bash
+python3 -m pytest -q ros2_ws/src/cpp_robotics_sim_ros/test/test_v014_harness_utilities.py ros2_ws/src/cpp_robotics_sim_ros/test/test_v014_mode_transition_skeleton.py
+./scripts/build.sh
+./scripts/test.sh
+```
+
+Implement REQ-031–038 and TC-0043–0056: dependency graph, admission guards, transaction serialization, rollback, active-goal transition policy, and dependency-loss degradation. Do not redesign lifecycle/readiness, change TF ownership, begin sensor-health/EKF scope, or weaken v0.1.3 gates.
